// scripts/cbm3-self-closeout.mjs
//
// CBM-3 self-validation closeout — the card's OWN bundle is generated by the
// PRODUCTION Graph closeout hook（runSubagentGraph → runColimaGraph →
// runMandatoryGraphCloseout → runCloseoutGate）, NOT by a hand-written source
// or a manual CLI invocation.
//
// The graph is the REAL review/repair ceremony:
//   SA-R1 ‖ SA-R2 -> SA-W1 -> SA-V1
//   SA-W1 lifecycle: writer (attempt 0) -> INDEPENDENT review agent -> PASS
//   （or bounded REPAIR, budget 1）-> re-review -> verifier.
// The mandatory closeout hook then auto-generates the CBM-3 bundle from the
// structured graph result + git-derived repo identity and — per the RB-1H
// hard rule — atomically delivers it to the fixed external-review surface
// ~/Desktop/AutoLoop-Review/Current/.
//
// The graph ALSO wires the CBM-3 read-only memory provider（dogfooding the
// production Graph integration; memory is DATA context only）. A missing
// store yields EMPTY_MEMORY（graph continues）; a corrupt store holds
// MEMORY_STORE_INVALID. Zero automatic write-back is asserted by the focused
// suite and the colima writeback test.
//
// Run: node scripts/cbm3-self-closeout.mjs
//      node scripts/cbm3-self-closeout.mjs --regenerate
//        --regenerate reuses the session's existing graph-closeout-evidence
//        (no colima re-run) and regenerates the bundle with the performance
//        probe evidence included, delivering it to the fixed surface after
//        the previous generation is rotated by the operator.

